From 23158559f29cfeecab129b1afc2adc9e9bf63540 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 18:33:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Run DS4.1's lagged mHC on TileKernels in the TileLang backend

TileKernels' post and stream collapse serve as they are. Each sublayer's
entry is two TileLang kernels: one per hidden block folds the previous
output into the streams, accumulates the projection's split partials on
TF32 tensor cores (DeepGEMM's precision, which does not run on SM12x) and
collapses the streams with the incoming pre-mix; one per token runs
TileKernels' reduce, mix split and Sinkhorn, emitting the new pre-mix,
beside the collapse's RMSNorm. The split and token tile are fixed, so a
token's results do not depend on the batch. Decoder layers now hold their
mHC as 'mhc', from the kernel family.
